Phase 3 verification report (FR-3 next-episode autoplay)

Commands and outcomes:
- flutter analyze -> No issues found! (ran in 4.8s)
- CI=true flutter test -> 374 passed, 0 failed (baseline 356, +18 new)

What shipped:
- lib/features/playback/playback_queue.dart (new): PlaybackQueueItem,
  buildEpisodeQueue (season order then following seasons), and the persisted
  autoplay preference backed by shared_preferences.
- lib/features/playback/playback_screen.dart: 'queue' parameter, _UpNextCard
  with a 15 s countdown plus Play now and Cancel, in-route advance that
  re-fetches the manifest, and real wiring for the previously dead skip-next
  and Next Episode controls.
- lib/features/playback/playback_navigation.dart: queue plumbed through the
  route extra plus readPlaybackQueueFromExtra, which drops malformed entries.
- lib/core/router/app_router.dart: parses the queue at the untyped route edge.
- lib/features/library/series_detail_screen.dart: builds the queue from the
  already-loaded series detail, so no server work was needed.
- lib/features/settings/settings_screen.dart: the Autoplay next episode toggle.
- test/features/playback/autoplay_test.dart (new): 18 tests.

Red state before the phase: 'No named parameter with the name queue'. The
nextEpisode callback, the Next Episode button, and the skip-next transport
button all existed and no caller ever passed one, so the capability was dead.

One real defect found and fixed by the test for the toggle: the screen read the
preference at completion time with 'dataOrNull ?? true', which reads as ENABLED
while the provider is still loading. A viewer who had turned autoplay off would
still have been advanced. The preference is now read once at start and the
check fails closed while the value is unknown.

Safety properties pinned by tests: nothing starts before the countdown expires;
any key press cancels it and leaves the card up; Play now starts immediately;
Cancel returns to the completed overlay; the toggle off starts nothing; movies
never advance; the last episode offers no next control.

Why: the owner asked for Netflix-style next autoplay.
